.Dd July 15, 2026
.Dt __OS_ERRNO 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm __os_errno_map ,
.Nm __os_errno_set_hook ,
.Nm __os_errno_get_hook
.Nd canonical errno to XTC_E_* translation with an embedder hook
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In os_errno.h
.Ft int
.Fn __os_errno_map "int posix_errno"
.Ft void
.Fn __os_errno_set_hook "int (*fn)(int posix_errno)"
.Ft "int (*)(int)"
.Fn __os_errno_get_hook void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The XTC runtime works exclusively in the
.Dv XTC_E_*
error space.
This module is the one place a raw POSIX
.Va errno
crosses into it: OS-layer wrappers call
.Fn __os_errno_map
at the syscall boundary instead of hand-rolling a per-file switch.
.Pp
.Fn __os_errno_map
translates
.Fa posix_errno
into a stable
.Dv XTC_E_*
code.
It is only ever consulted on a known failure, so an unrecognized value,
or 0, maps to
.Dv XTC_E_IO
.Pq an I/O-class error the runtime does not further distinguish ,
never a success code.
Callers that need
.Dv XTC_OK
check the syscall return value
.Em before
calling this.
The built-in table maps, among others,
.Dv EINVAL
and
.Dv EEXIST
to
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL ,
.Dv ENOMEM
to
.Dv XTC_E_NOMEM ,
.Dv ENOENT
to
.Dv XTC_E_NOTFOUND ,
.Dv EAGAIN
and
.Dv EWOULDBLOCK
to
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN ,
.Dv ECANCELED
to
.Dv XTC_E_ABORTED ,
.Dv ENOSYS
to
.Dv XTC_E_NOSYS ,
and
.Dv ERANGE
to
.Dv XTC_E_RANGE .
.Pp
.Fn __os_errno_set_hook
installs an optional embedder hook, consulted by
.Fn __os_errno_map
.Em before
the built-in table.
An embedder that shims the underlying syscalls
.Pq a custom VFS, a hosted or sandboxed libc
uses this to override the translation.
The hook receives the raw
.Fa errno
and returns an
.Dv XTC_E_*
code, or 0 to fall through to the built-in table.
Installing
.Dv NULL
restores the default
.Pq built-in table only .
.Pp
.Fn __os_errno_get_hook
returns the currently installed hook, or
.Dv NULL
if none.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn __os_errno_map
returns an
.Dv XTC_E_*
code
.Pq always negative or, by convention, never Dv XTC_OK .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
All three functions are safe to call concurrently from any thread; the
hook pointer is published with a single atomic store.
Embedders normally install the hook once at startup, before other
threads run.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Translate a failed
.Fn open :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int fd = open(path, O_RDONLY);
if (fd < 0)
        return __os_errno_map(errno);
.Ed
.Pp
Override the mapping from a sandbox shim:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static int my_map(int e) {
        if (e == EACCES)
                return XTC_E_RESOURCE;  /* sandbox denial */
        return 0;                       /* defer to the built-in table */
}
__os_errno_set_hook(my_map);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr __os_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_strerror 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
First appeared in xtc 1.24.0 (M1.5).
